{"full":"hf:ZhengmingYu/dmad","spaceId":"ZhengmingYu/dmad","name":"DMAD — 4-step MiniMax-H3 student","source":"huggingface","description":"4-step text-to-audio-video generation, distilled from H3","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","mcp-server","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":5,"created":"2026-10-03T08:15:33.000Z","updated":"2026-10-03T09:24:59.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://zhengmingyu-dmad.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/ZhengmingYu/dmad","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:43.863Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:43.863Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:43.863Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🎬","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DMAD (Yu et al., 2610.02188 · project · code · weights) distills a multi-step teacher into few-step students by matching the distribution of the student's samples to the teacher's — no data, no extra inference cost. This Space serves the released 4-step MiniMax-H3 student: a rank-128 LoRA over the 33B omni-modal H3 transformer that turns the 50-step teacher into a 4-step generator of 1344x768 video with a synchronized stereo soundtrack.","Everything here is inference only — the demo runs the distilled student with the paper's own re-noise sampler, not the training procedure.","MiniMax-H3 is 195.9 GiB in bfloat16 and a ZeroGPU Space is evicted at 150 GB of storage, so one Space cannot hold it unquantized. The 62.14 GiB Qwen3-VL conditioner runs in multimodalart/qwen3vl-conditioner; this Space calls its /encode over the gradio API per request and holds the transformer + both VAEs (77.3 GB download). The wire format — promptembeds (layer-50 Qwen3-VL hidden states, prompt verbatim) + texttokentags — is exactly what dmadh3.encodeprompt produces, i.e. what the student was trained on. Both Spaces pin the same 1344x768 canvas."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/